  "notes": [
   "Only forecasts made before each player's own kickoff count, from the immutable run store; a forecast made or rerun after kickoff is never scored, and nothing is reconstructed after the fact.",
   "Only fully final NFL weeks are evidence. Player-weeks of weeks still in progress are listed as preliminary, without a verdict.",
   "Only each week's own pregame forecast (horizon 0) is scored. Rest-of-season forecasts made weeks earlier (horizon 1 or more) are never mixed in, even when the site shows one for a week without a newer run.",
   "Unconditional comparison (the headline): every resolved player-week the model projected; a player who did not play scores 0, as in a real lineup. The conditional comparison (players who appeared) is reported separately.",
   "Paired: ESPN and the model are scored on exactly the same player-weeks. Players the model could not project show ESPN's number on the site; those fallback rows are counted but never credited to the model.",
   "MAE difference = MAE(ours) - MAE(ESPN): negative means our projections were closer. The interval resamples whole NFL weeks, because player-weeks of one week are correlated; an interval that includes 0 means no established difference.",
   "Mean signed error = mean(actual - projection): positive means the projection was too low on average.",
   "RB accuracy is also split by pregame volume (carries + targets per game over the back's last games, threshold 4): the model is expected to lose to simpler forecasts on low-volume backs and win with volume, so the pooled RB figure mixes two opposite effects. Each group faces the same evidence bar as a position."
